{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dhk7fzinhczlqapdnecf4hcyj7w6emrimutntgqqud7ela6ok4uq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- [x] **SYMBOLS.md** — `nm -D` diff between the two `.so`s is **empty** (6/6: `create_buffer`, `append_to_buffer`, `destroy_buffer`, `get_operation_name`, `perform_operation`, `buffapp`). 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols. No module was skipped in translation.\n- [x] **Phase B** — all **27 CONFIGS.md rows** pass across randomized inputs (fixed seeds).\n- [x] **Binary stdout** — no driver executable exists (`CMakeLists.txt` builds only a SHARED lib), so `buffapp`'s `printf` output is compared byte-for-byte instead (rows C21–C27).\n- [x] **Phase C** — all **26 ERRORS.md rows** have passing differential tests (27 test fns), incl. NULL pointers, zero/oversized/negative lengths, one-past-range values, and out-of-range enum ints.\n- [x] **All feature combinations** — Cargo.toml declares no `[features]`; verified under default, `--no-default-features`, and additionally the dev-profile `cdylib`.\n\n## Bug found and fixed\n\n**Dev-profile `cdylib` diverged on the NULL-dereference path** in `append_to_buffer` (`src/lib.rs:126`). Rust's debug `ub_checks` turned the raw-pointer deref into a non-unwinding panic → **SIGABRT (6)**, while the C raises **SIGSEGV (11)**. Fixed by disabling `debug-assertions`/`overflow-checks` in `[profile.dev]` (the C is compiled without UB instrumentation; all arithmetic in `lib.rs` is already explicitly `wrapping_*`). Only surfaced because tests compare fatal signals as first-class results.\n\n## Notable derivations\n\n- **ERRORS.md E24** looked unreachable but isn't: `buffapp` traps on `result / intermediate3` when `intermediate3 == -1` and `result == INT_MIN`. Solving `i1·i2 ≡ -1 (mod 2³²)` ∧ `i1+i2 ≡ INT_MIN` gives `buffapp(0, 1073741823, 0, 1073741825)` → confirmed **SIGFPE in both*